.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt QUOTACHECK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quotacheck
.Nd count disk usage for quotas
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl v
.Fl a | Ar filesystem ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
walks a volume and counts, for each user and group, the space its files
take (allocated blocks) and how many files it has, a hard-linked file
once.
It writes the counts to the volume's
.Pa .quota.user
and
.Pa .quota.group ,
keeping the limits there, and makes them when they are missing.
While quotas are on, the kernel gets the new counts too.
Files of the super-user and of group 0 are not counted.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Every mounted local volume that wants quotas (has
.Pa .quota.ops.user
or
.Pa .quota.ops.group
at its root).
.It Fl g
Group quotas only.
.It Fl u
User quotas only.
.It Fl v
Say what is checked and what changed.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl g
or
.Fl u ,
the types the volume wants; with them, those types, even if it does not.
Only the super-user may run it.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quota 1 ,
.Xr quotactl 2 ,
.Xr edquota 8 ,
.Xr quotaon 8 ,
.Xr repquota 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
